From e017b5fdc7c5155993c5c41016151e831eec13ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airebuild <k@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:05:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(ai): real backend ladder, Gemini 3.x config, honest
 provenance

Three defects, all of which made the AI layer quietly useless.

1. Gemini structured output failed on every call.
   The config sent ThinkingConfig(thinking_budget=0). Gemini 3.x replaced
   that integer with a thinking_level enum and defaults to medium, so
   thinking was never disabled; reasoning tokens consumed
   max_output_tokens and generateContent returned finish_reason=MAX_TOKENS
   with empty text. Now sends thinking_level (default minimal) and drops
   temperature/top_p/top_k, which are deprecated on 3.x.

2. There was no ladder. get_ai_backend() picked exactly one backend and a
   failure went straight to template. Groq was never implemented at all
   despite being the intended primary. Now: groq -> gemini -> ollama ->
   template, each with one strict retry, overridable via AI_BACKENDS.
   Groq speaks the OpenAI-compatible endpoint over httpx.
   Default GROQ_MODEL is openai/gpt-oss-120b: Groq deprecated
   llama-3.3-70b-versatile on 17 Jun 2026 and names this the migration.

3. Provenance was fabricated. ingest/job.py hardcoded generated_by as
   gemini and model_version as gemini-2.5-flash on every AI-generated
   advisory, so an Ollama-written advisory claimed Gemini and the recorded
   model id was one the code never called. Both now come from the backend
   that actually produced the text; the Literal and the TypeScript union
   were widened to match.

Also: Gemini's synchronous generate_content now runs in asyncio.to_thread
so it stops blocking the event loop, debug dumps moved off logger.error,
and fenced json replies are tolerated.

17 new tests (110 total, was 93) covering ladder order, fallthrough on a
dead backend, rejection of a hallucinating backend, and the containment
gate on Devanagari and Bengali numerals.
---
