From 3ca4cc6bbddf865ed01f410b3e3dc98b80107457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airebuild <k@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:18:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(backend): close fail-open auth, surface synthetic
 weather, plug leaks

Three findings from a sweep of the data and routing layer.

1. Internal endpoints failed open. _check_token skipped the check in two
   ways: DEMO_MODE defaults to "true", so a deploy that never set it left
   /internal/seed reachable by path alone; and even with DEMO_MODE=false
   an empty INTERNAL_TOKEN bypassed the comparison entirely, so forgetting
   the secret removed the lock instead of jamming it shut. Outside demo a
   missing token now returns 503 and the comparison is constant-time.

2. Synthetic weather was served indistinguishably from measured weather.
   fetch_grid falls back to generate_mock_forecast on any error, which is
   a fine trade for availability. But the rules engine attaches the same
   real ICAR citation either way, so a farmer reading a SEVERE warning had
   no way to tell whether the rainfall behind it was observed or invented.
   GET /weather/{grid_id} now returns sources and has_synthetic_data, and
   the dashboard shows a warning above the risk strip, in all four
   languages, before any advisory is read.

3. fetch_grid leaked an httpx.AsyncClient on every call that did not get
   one passed in, and generate_mock_forecast seeded from hash(grid_id),
   which CPython randomises per process, so its "deterministic per grid"
   forecast changed on every restart.

13 new tests (123 total, was 110) covering demo bypass, missing and wrong
tokens, token prefixes, and weather provenance including partial
contamination and stale records outside the served window.
